WEBVTT

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.210
I was able to make
delicious rice again today!

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:27.660
Welcome home!

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.870
I'm back!

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.130
Hey!

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.940
Oof!

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.660
Isn't the way you're using the ax dangerous?

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.660
You think?

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.080
It's too wild.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.700
You get unnecessarily tired
like that, don't you?

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.960
First, stick half of the ax into the wood.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:12.130
Next, bring it up together with the wood.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:13.210
And then swing it down.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:14.750
See?

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:17.710
Yeah.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.050
There!

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:24.470
Oof!

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.020
It's a nice day today...

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.820
Are you happy now, Machi?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.160
Why are you talking like that?

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:46.870
I'm not chopping wood to
vent my stress or anything.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.620
This is nowhere near enough firewood.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.750
Every day, we cook and heat the bath.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.670
No matter how much
we have, it's not enough.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:01.010
If we use a rice cooker, a hot-water system, and
an induction stove, we don't have to chop wood.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.680
Machi...

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:07.390
We have no gas at our house...

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:13.190
...because this house is in a place where
it is very hard to transport propane gas.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.560
But we do have electricity, you know.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.440
Why don't you make better use of it?

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:24.110
It's nice and charming to live
on firewood in this day and age...

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.160
...but I think it's a waste of our time and effort.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:32.750
Only an old woman, a girl
and a bear live in this house.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.790
It's about time for you to turn your eyes
to the convenience of electricity.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.460
Stop talking and get back to work, Natsu.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.680
She's been chopping wood
on Fuchi's orders all these years...

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.140
Amayadori

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:50.720
Oof!

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.270
...without making a single displeased face.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.020
Could there be some
important meaning to it?

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.690
There must be some
important meaning to it...

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:05.910
Some meaning...

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.200
Is it possible...?

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.500
Is this... your hobby?

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.170
Of course not.
What are you saying?

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.210
Of course not...

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.250
Then why?

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.710
I don't wanna do it, either, to be honest.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.050
This is such a hard labor.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:25.880
But...

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.590
...you know...

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:32.060
Appliances can be pretty hard to use.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.720
They aren't cheap, either.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:39.150
Well, if a rice cooker is left right in front
of me, I don't mind trying to use it.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.110
But there isn't one.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:41.820
There is!

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.900
This is one of the latest models
of induction heating rice cookers!

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.570
Where did you get it?

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.780
What's with <i>this</i>?

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.870
Yoshio has a connection at an
appliance store, and they gave it to him.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.290
I see...

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.210
It's an expensive one!

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.500
It can make delicious rice!

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.130
I see...

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.920
You can make rice quickly and
easily every day from now on!

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:08.800
Now, Machi... open it.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.400
Machi?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.410
Wh-Which button should I press?

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:44.920
Well then, why don't we
try making some rice?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.440
It's not hot yet, Machi.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:02.770
But what if I get an electric shock?

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.270
You won't.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.820
It's not even in the rice cooker anymore.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:11.030
There's no electricity left in it?

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.070
No. No electricity is left.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.280
Nothing left, nothing left.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.240
Looks like it'll take a while.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:18.830
Okay.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.080
Now that you're done rinsing the rice,
let's put it back in the rice cooker.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.340
That won't work!

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:52.660
Water! Water!

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.240
We need a fire extinguisher!

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.080
Just as I thought, I couldn't do it...

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:04.250
I shouldn't have touched a machine
with this many buttons!

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.840
You didn't even touch any buttons yet!

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.550
And move away from there!

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:12.010
I'm a kumamiko and a maiden
of misfortune at the same time...

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.970
She's a maiden of misfortune!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.140
Maiden of misfortune!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.180
When did you get a name like that?!

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.180
It's not possible...

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.810
I can't do it...

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.190
Don't give up, Machi.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:25.940
It won't do, Machi.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:27.400
Don't give up.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:33.650
People in the city make full use
of variable-pressure IH rice cookers.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.990
They make pudding and stuff
by using the different functions.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.290
With a rice cooker?

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.670
Do you think... I can do it, too?

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:50.880
Thank you, Natsu.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.800
I think... I'll keep trying a bit more!

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.480
A rice cooker...!

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.990
Just as you'd expect from a rice cooker,
I feel like the rice tastes different.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:18.450
The heat was uniformly distributed.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.280
This is, indeed, the blessing of electricity!

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:22.870
You didn't use electricity.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.330
You used a fire!

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:30.090
A rice cooker is nice because the rice
doesn't stick to the bottom of the pot.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:33.010
Yeah, since it's PTFE-coated.

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.590
Oh... PTFE-coated, huh?

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:39.350
You only used the inner pot.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.560
This doesn't mean that you
were able to use a rice cooker.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.850
And don't treat just the
inner pot as a rice cooker.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:47.690
Natsu is annoying.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:51.820
Considering that you're like this,
you using a cell phone is nothing but a dream.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.150
I'm done eating.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.910
Now, hurry up and eat!

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.410
Once you're done eating,
we'll do more wood-chopping!

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.370
We haven't finish today's quota yet.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.330
I wanna go home and watch TV...

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:20.050
Work hard! Work hard!
It's only early evening!

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:24.310
From a temple,

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:27.560
a ghost appears floating.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:31.810
Behind the ghost,

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:35.530
a chicken seller appears,
saying, "Cock-a-doodle-doo."

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:39.150
Behind the chicken seller,

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:42.620
a thief appears, saying,
"Hand over your money."

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:46.250
Behind the thief,

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:49.710
a policeman appears,
saying, "Pistol, pistol."

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.170
One, two, three!

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.000
I lost!

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.840
Ahh! I lost!

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:59.220
Yaay! Yaay!

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:00.510
Oh, no!

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:04.310
Yaay! I won! I won!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:01.890
I lost three times in a row...

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.350
You guys really get along well, don't you?

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.810
Oh, Yoshio, you were here?

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.350
Oh, Yoshio-kun, you were here?

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:14.480
In any case, you two should be more vigilant.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.190
But we're so bored.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:20.780
We rarely hold rituals where
the villagers gather, so...

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:24.740
What about you, Yoshio - you're here a lot.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.950
What about you, Yoshio-kun - you're here a lot.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.700
Are you really doing your job?

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:29.000
Hey, hey, that's not nice.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:35.420
I work for the village office, but before that,
I have an important duty as a miko-caretaker!

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:36.750
I didn't know that.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:36.960
Is that so?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.170
I thought he had nothing else to do.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:44.090
So just because no one's
watching you, you can't-

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.090
Hello?!

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:45.970
Anybody home?!

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.640
Old man Hashida!

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:49.680
What is it?

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.520
Oh, hey, Yoshio!

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.890
Oh, it's you Yoshio?

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.610
Fuchi asked me to bring this here.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.150
You'll use it today, right?

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:02.820
Oh, yeah.

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.320
Thanks!

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.450
Looks like Fuchi isn't around today, huh?

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.990
Do your best, okay?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.290
Yep, yep, yep, yep

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.410
Uhm...

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:12.330
Say...

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.380
...this is the sake to be put on the altar, right?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.550
Oh, was it the wrong brand or something?

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.050
No, not at all!

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:22.050
Looks like Machi is eager to do it.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.430
Then Natsu must be relieved, too.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.510
We'll pay attention and listen to him.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:29.100
Yep, yep, yep.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.480
Listen up and listen good.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.060
Okay?

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.690
I see, I see.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:37.060
So young people can hold
rituals by themselves, huh?

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.270
I feel quite moved.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.780
Well, you know...

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.950
Welcome back, Yoshio.

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.070
Welcome back, Yoshio-kun.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.240
What did old man Hashida say?

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.000
It seems like we're doing something today.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.000
Huh?

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:53.620
What?!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.920
"It seems like we're doing something"?

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.130
We weren't told anything about it.

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:00.420
Well, neither was I.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.760
Granny must have planned it.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.510
Grandma went to Mt. Osore\for a hot spring cure.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.470
Well, since she's old, I guess it's possible

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:11.560
that she forgot to tell us about it
and just went to the hot spring.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:12.930
Wh-What're we gonna do?

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:16.310
Having you in charge will only
turn it into a disaster, Yoshio!

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:16.520
Having you in charge will only
turn it into a disaster, Yoshio-kun!

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:17.810
That's rude.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:20.650
Anyway... we'd better make it
work somehow by ourselves.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.070
But...

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:24.030
Cancel it, let's cancel it!

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:26.700
We have to know what kind
of ritual it's supposed to be.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.910
It can't be the summer purification, right?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:33.540
He sounded like they're going to
gather here at the main shrine.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:38.500
Okay then!

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.420
I'm gonna go gather information anyway.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.300
You guys set up the altar
and the drapes, okay?!

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.340
Oh, and floor cushions, too!

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.680
We can't do it!

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:58.230
Let's wait until Grandma comes home!

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.020
Stop complaining!

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.910
There's no food for the offering.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:14.290
It looks empty.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:17.960
What shall we do?

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:21.960
It can't be helped.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.880
Let's put out some snacks.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:25.380
Man...

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:29.930
In a normal shrine, they'd have many things
to put out, like mirrors and such.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.010
It would have been so cool if we had
the Three Sacred Treasures, huh?

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.680
By the way, Miss Machi...

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.680
By the way, Machi-san...

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:39.600
What are the three sacred treasures
at home after World War II?

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:43.070
A refrigerator, a washing machine, and a TV!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:43.980
Correct.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:48.650
Although you haven't been able
to make full use of any of them.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:50.110
Now, wait a minute!

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:52.620
I can make a full use of the refrigerator!

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.330
Isn't there anything else to put out?

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:56.370
Wait!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.000
Well...

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.630
This will definitely get us
in even more trouble.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.130
This is amazing!

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:07.920
How do you use this?

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.550
Don't touch it!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:10.800
I'm back!

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:12.430
Whoa...

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:16.220
It's starting to look like a ritual setup.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:18.230
Oh, welcome back, Yoshio.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:19.230
Hm?

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.150
Well...

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.520
This isn't right.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.230
Yeah... I know.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.280
I know, but...

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:29.900
Today's ritual isn't about the mountain gods.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:30.700
Machi.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.290
So the altar comes here.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.500
And Natsu sits there.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:45.540
So did you find out what ritual
we'll be holding today after all?

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:46.340
Yeah.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:48.300
After I asked around,
I did some research...

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.050
...it's probably this.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.050
"Kikase."

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:57.100
It's a ceremony in which Kumai's representative
recites a prayer as the messenger of the gods.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.850
It's also a meeting for him to show the villagers his
ability to speak as if he was possessed by the gods.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:06.860
By the way, the record says that
the last one was held thirty years ago.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:09.740
Why did Fuchi dig up something like that?!

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:10.820
Beats me.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:14.070
She might have thought
that we needed it now.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:15.200
What?

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:20.580
Ah!

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:24.670
She became relaxed once she realized
that she won't have to do much!

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:28.090
Machi still has to recite a
prayer or something, right?!

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.170
No.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.550
I don't see anything like that written in here...

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.470
But if she does, it would look
even more like a ritual!

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:35.010
We should do it!

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.850
Oops, look at the time!

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:42.980
So be flexible.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:46.900
There you have it, so make things work
according to the situation, okay?

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.070
Hey, wait.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.150
What am I supposed to talk
about from the platform?

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:51.900
You do have cue cards, right?

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:53.360
Oh...

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.200
Improvise!

00:16:58.620 --> 00:16:59.370
Natsu...

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.410
Good luck.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:28.110
Hello.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:33.280
Thank you very much for
gathering here today for a bear.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:38.280
With your permission, I, a bear,
would like to give a speech.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.660
I hope you will listen.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:44.290
A number of years has already passed
since I became the representative of Kumai.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.670
While I'm still inexperienced,

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:50.170
I've been somehow performing
rituals together with...

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.680
...together with the miko, but...

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.050
Uhm...

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:05.020
The peace of this village is supposed
to depend on our front legs.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:11.110
So please don't forget that you're
always back to back with misfortune.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.490
This is a small village.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:23.950
If you fail to have faith, Kumai,
a naturally impetuous deity, will destroy it.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.250
Weak humans.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.250
Throw yourselves at my fangs and claws.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:35.960
No, that's not it.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:39.050
What I really want to say is that...

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:43.560
...due to the spread of transportation
technology and the Internet in recent years,

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:47.480
you're now able to obtain what
you want without going out.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.400
Books, food, appliances...

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:53.770
You can purchase all sorts of things
no matter what kind of products they are

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.610
and receive the most advanced services.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.240
Hence, you don't have to go to the city.

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:05.700
Also, credit cards are nothing to be scared of.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:10.500
If you use them properly,
you won't be dragged into trouble...

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.420
...and they come with many bonuses.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:18.170
So stop fantasizing about the city,
which lacks substance...

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:21.680
...and try making the fullest use of the Internet...

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:25.260
...so that you don't have to abandon
this village you love so much.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.070
That was wonderful.

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.780
That's our Master Natsu.

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:36.980
That's our Natsu-sama.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:39.030
It's a blessing.

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:47.080
Hm?

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:47.950
Is it over?

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:49.250
Machi...

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.420
Were you listening to my speech?

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.170
Nope, not at all.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:57.340
Okay, the meal after the ritual will be
served at the soba restaurant Oniroku!

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:01.380
I was really looking forward to this.

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:04.680
So what was today's ritual about?

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:06.010
I guess it doesn't matter.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:12.230
Isn't there something?

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.770
I'm back!

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.570
Can't you think of something?

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.910
Maybe not...

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:30.700
There is!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:31.910
There's a lot!

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:36.460
There are apples, pears, grapes, Japanese apricots,
potatoes, rice, and wild vegetables.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:39.920
And the rice cakes the old lady who lives
next door makes taste super good, too!

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:42.720
Isn't there anything that has a stronger brand?

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.720
Who cares about brand strength?!

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:46.720
Their tastiness can be accepted nationwide!

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:49.890
Nationwide? No way!

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:50.100
No way it's nationwide.

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.430
He's right.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:54.060
This is a dull village
that has nothing to offer.

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:56.810
Eh?

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:00.400
Miss Yasuda, be more confident!

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:00.570
Yasuda-san, be more confident!

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:03.240
Wh-Wh-What're you talking about?!

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.410
You're not someone who's just dull.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.370
If you present yourself properly,
you can find yourself someone special!

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:14.080
That's sexual harassment!

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:19.840
Manager, what this village lacks are
confidence, pride, and presentation!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.090
That's all!

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.090
Kumade Village

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.090
Village
Revitalization
Contest

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.090
Ideas Wanted!

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.220
Then you work on it,
okay, Amayadori?

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:24.420
Then you work on it,
okay, Amayadori-kun?

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:25.180
Huh?

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:27.640
The village revitalization contest.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.930
I want to show our superiors
we're really working on it at least.

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:37.940
You don't have to make it a big deal
as long as you make us look good.

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.110
Amayadori?

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.690
Amayadori-kun?

00:21:43.490 --> 00:21:46.450
You don't have to take it
so seriously, okay?

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:48.370
Leave it to me!

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:28.300
I'm hungr-

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:30.720
We will explain a shrine term today.

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:33.550
"Shinsen."

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:37.680
It's a general term for the food
and wine offered to the gods.

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:44.110
Normally people choose from sake,
rice cake, and seasonal produce.

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:47.150
Munch, munch, munch...

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:46.980
Machi...

00:23:47.150 --> 00:23:49.780
Crunch, crunch, crunch, crunch...

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:49.530
Wait until the ceremony is over to eat, okay?

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:50.740
Munch...

00:23:51.110 --> 00:23:54.870
Kumamiko.
